    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can offer personalized tutoring, explain concepts in simple language, and provide instant feedback. They can adapt to different learning styles, like helping visual learners with diagrams or helping those who struggle with language. In schools, they could support teachers by generating practice problems or simplifying difficult topics—making math more approachable and less intimidating."
